@tghosth - I think we don't have covered this

From: https://github.com/OWASP/ASVS/issues/1603#issuecomment-1497625275

> My thought is that when testing a web app, we would document a finding for any occurrence of a link to http: if that page supports https: thus avoiding the user experiencing redirect to https:. A code change would be needed to fix.

I opened PR (#1898 ) to solve two requirements from the discussion here.

@securitydave - at the moment we don't address the original requirement or problem statement from the opened issue. Although I agree that technically it could improve the security, in practice it is a bit too niche for ASVS.

If you feel, that it is really important and widespread problem enough, we can consider covering it in the recommendations section.
